  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given NNN nodes numbered from 111 to NNN.\n\nThe score\\texttt{score}score of the task is initially 000.\n\nYou are given QQQ queries of the following type:\n\n\nGiven integers uuu and vvv:\n\nAdd an edge between nodes x=(score⊕u)x = (\\texttt{score} \\oplus u)x=(score⊕u) and y=(score⊕v)y = (\\texttt{score} \\oplus v)y=(score⊕v). It is guaranteed that both xxx and yyy belong to different components and 1≤x,y≤N1\\le x, y\\le N1≤x,y≤N.\nAfter adding the edge, let ddd denote the **sum** of diameters of all components.\n\nUpdate the score\\texttt{score}score as score=score⊕d\\texttt{score} = \\texttt{score} \\oplus dscore=score⊕d, where ⊕\\oplus⊕ denotes the bitwise xor operation.\n\n\nFind the final score\\texttt{score}score after all the queries.\n\nNote:\n\n\nAll nodes are considered as individual components initially. Thus, their diameters are 000.\nThe diameter of a component with more than one node is defined as the **maximum** distance between any two nodes in that component.\nThe distance between two nodes is the number of edges in the simple path between the nodes.\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line contains a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of multiple lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains two space-separated integers NNN and QQQ denoting number of nodes and queries respectively.\nThe next QQQ lines describe the queries. The ithi^{th}ith of these QQQ lines contain:\n\nuuu vvv : Two space-separated integers representing the query.\n\n\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line, the final value of score\\texttt{score}score.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1001 \\leq T \\leq 1001≤T≤100",
      "1≤N,Q≤1051 \\leq N, Q \\leq 10^51≤N,Q≤105",
      "0≤ui,vi≤2⋅N,ui≠vi0 \\leq u_i, v_i \\leq 2\\cdot N, u_i \\neq v_i 0≤ui​,vi​≤2⋅N,ui​=vi​",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases won't exceed 10510^5105."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "1\n3 2\n1 2\n3 2",
        "output": "3",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: Given 333 nodes and number 222 queries. The score\\texttt{score}score is initially 000.\n\nQuery 111: Add edge between nodes 0⊕1=10\\oplus 1 = 10⊕1=1 and 0⊕2=20\\oplus 2 = 20⊕2=2. There are 222 components now ({1,2},{3})(\\{1,2\\}, \\{3\\})({1,2},{3}). One component has diameter 111 and other has diameter 000. The sum of diameters is 111. Thus, we update score=score⊕1=1\\texttt{score} = \\texttt{score} \\oplus 1 = 1score=score⊕1=1.\nQuery 222: Add edge between nodes 1⊕3=21\\oplus 3 = 21⊕3=2 and 1⊕2=31\\oplus 2 = 31⊕2=3. There is 111 component now ({1,2,3})(\\{1,2,3\\})({1,2,3}). The component has diameter 222. Thus, the sum of diameters is 222. The updated score is score=score⊕2=3\\texttt{score} = \\texttt{score} \\oplus 2 = 3score=score⊕2=3.\n\nHence final value of score\\texttt{score}score is 333."
      }
    ]
  },
